{
  "id": "u07-l02",
  "unit": "u07-directions",
  "title": "Left, right, straight",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Directions use the polite command **যান** (*jan*) 'go': **ডানে যান** 'go right', **বামে যান** 'go left', **সোজা যান** 'go straight'.\n\n**মোড়** (*mor*) — intersection / corner — is the key landmark word in Bangladeshi cities. **মোড়ে বামে যান** = 'turn left at the intersection'.\n\n**দিয়ে** after a noun means 'along / through': **এই রাস্তা দিয়ে সোজা যান** 'go straight along this road'.\n\n**Kolkata:** people more often say **ডানদিকে** / **বাঁদিকে** ('to the right side / left side').",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "dane",
      "bn": "ডানে",
      "tr": "dane",
      "en": "right"
    },
    {
      "id": "bame",
      "bn": "বামে",
      "tr": "bame",
      "en": "left"
    },
    {
      "id": "shoja",
      "bn": "সোজা",
      "tr": "shoja",
      "en": "straight",
      "notes": "Also an adjective: 'straight, simple, easy'."
    },
    {
      "id": "jan",
      "bn": "যান",
      "tr": "jan",
      "en": "go (polite)",
      "notes": "Polite command of যাওয়া 'go'; same form = present 'you (polite) go'. Familiar যাও, intimate যা."
    },
    {
      "id": "rasta",
      "bn": "রাস্তা",
      "tr": "rasta",
      "en": "road"
    },
    {
      "id": "diye",
